{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:ade9673ee1f166e6","name":"Tactician Battle Computer","source":{"id":"source:reference-ade9673ee1f166e6","title":"Tactician Battle Computer","revision":21119,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T01:11:44Z","sha256":"86981bfce148d545979d5935a8b3835856aa951b44a997fc115b8b3c9c628129","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=21119","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Tactician%20Battle%20Computer&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-ade9673ee1f166e6","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scavenger's Guide to Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scavenger%27s_Guide_to_Droids"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Cost:"]}," 5,000\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Weight:"]}," 10 Kilograms\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Strict governmental regulations apply to ",{"tag":"a","children":["4th-Degree Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/4th-Degree_Droids","referenceId":"reference:e0ba1be2d9a6a37a"},". However, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Manufacturers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Manufacturers","referenceId":"reference:41c1bfb8b5b00c0a"}," know that money can be made by manufacturing ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"}," for war, so they develop ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Systems"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Systems"}," such as the Tactician Battle Computer to circumvent restrictions on ",{"tag":"a","children":["4th-Degree Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/4th-Degree_Droids","referenceId":"reference:e0ba1be2d9a6a37a"},". This software package and transmitter can be installed on any ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid"},". Additionally, small transceivers must also be installed on the ranged weapons used with the package. Restrictions prohibit the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid"}," from using any weapons other than those with transceivers associated with its Tactician Battle Computer. In fact, if the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid"}," running the Tactician Battle Computer picks up a weapon not equipped with the transceiver, the Tactician Battle Computer shuts down and can be restarted only after succeeding on a DC 20 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," check.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid"}," spends a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Standard Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Standard_Action"}," to analyze the current battle conditions. The ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid"}," transmits its findings to the sensors installed on the weapons of its allies. The ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid"}," automatically grants a +2 bonus to the next attack roll made by a number of allies equal to its ",{"tag":"a","children":["Intelligence"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Intelligence"}," modifier (minimum 1). If an ally does not make its next attack before the end of its next turn, this bonus is lost. Only ranged weapons can be used with the Tactician Battle Computer.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
